		{
			"identifier": "MaryOBlock",
			"uid": 106884,
			"tags": [],
			"exportToToc": false,
			"allowOutOfBounds": true,
			"doc": "One of Mary-O's REACTIVE blocks — the ones that answer a head-bonk from below.  What it LOOKS like and what it HOLDS are separate fields, on purpose: a block that looks like a brick but really has a powerup is a thing you should be able to author. A block's look never announces its contents — that is why `Quasar` is no longer a look.  `kind` — what it looks like:    Question  a ?-block. Wears its own texture, and an inert one once spent. A quasar comes out of an ORDINARY ?-block.   Power     the old spelling of Question, kept in the list only so a file that already says it still loads. Prefer Question.   Brick     masonry. Breakable ONLY when it holds nothing — a loaded brick behaves like a ?-block wearing brick art, which is the classic behaviour.   Hidden    nothing at all until it is struck. It is NOT a floor: only a head coming up into it from below collides, so she cannot stand on it and cannot bump it from the side. (Becoming a visible solid once discovered is the classic behaviour and is NOT implemented yet.)  `contents` — what it holds. Leave it BLANK for the sensible default for that look (a Question levels toward the lantern, a Brick holds nothing, a Hidden holds a coin), or say:    Empty           nothing. A Brick that holds nothing is the one that breaks.   AlwaysWand      always the star wand, whatever form she is in.   AlwaysLantern   always the cinder beacon.   AlwaysQuasar    always a pocket quasar.   Coin            a coin, credited on the strike — no item to catch.   TowardWand      the next rung on the way to the wand.   TowardLantern   the next rung on the way to the lantern — small gets the wand, tall gets the lantern. This is what every ?-block in 1-1 does.  A pickup never makes her WEAKER: a wand collected by fire Mary-O pays coins instead of demoting her, whether it came from a block or was authored on the floor.  One tile, floating at bonk height over ground she can stand on. The block's collision and art come from this entity; nothing else has to be authored for it to work.  An unknown kind or an unknown contents is REFUSED at load rather than becoming a plain wall — a block that silently stopped being special still stops the player, so the level would look whole with one bonus quietly gone. `Quasar` as a kind is refused by name, and the message says what to write instead.",
			"tileOpacity": 1.0,
			"lineOpacity": 1.0,
			"fillOpacity": 0.08,
			"hollow": false,
			"color": "#E8A33D",
			"renderMode": "Tile",
			"showName": true,
			"tilesetId": 106934,
			"tileRenderMode": "Cover",
			"tileRect": { "tilesetUid": 106934, "x": 0, "y": 0, "w": 32, "h": 32 },
			"uiTileRect": { "tilesetUid": 106934, "x": 0, "y": 0, "w": 32, "h": 32 },
